<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt1326" id="mwCXA" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-roman","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:548}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:549}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:550}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:551}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:552}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:553}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:554}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:555}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:556}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:557}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:558}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCXE"><li about="#cite_note-traditional-25" id="cite_note-traditional-25" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCXI"><a href="#cite_ref-traditional_25-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCXM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCXQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-traditional-25" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Traditional.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-dir-rtl-28" id="cite_note-dir-rtl-28" data-mw-footnote-number="ii"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCXU"><a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCXY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCXc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCXg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCXk">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCXo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCXs">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-3" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCXw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCX0">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-4" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCX4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCX8">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dir-rtl_28-5" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCYE">6</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-dir-rtl-28" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Direction of text is right-to-left.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-rare-31" id="cite_note-rare-31" data-mw-footnote-number="iii"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCYI"><a href="#cite_ref-rare_31-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCYQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rare_31-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCYY">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rare_31-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCYg">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rare_31-3" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCYo">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-rare-31" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Rarely used.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-dash-33" id="cite_note-dash-33" data-mw-footnote-number="iv"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCYs"><a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCYw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCY0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCY4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCY8">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZE">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-3" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZM">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-4" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZU">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-5" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZc">6</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-6" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZk">7</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-7" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZs">8</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-8" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZ0">9</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-9" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCZ4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCZ8">10</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-10" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCaA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCaE">11</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-11" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCaI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCaM">12</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-12" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCaQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCaU">13</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-13" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCaY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCac">14</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-14" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCag"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCak">15</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-15" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCao"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCas">16</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-dash_33-16" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCaw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCa0">17</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-dash-33" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotation_dash" title="Quotation dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCa4">quotation dash</a> is preferred for dialogue.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-closing-35" id="cite_note-closing-35" data-mw-footnote-number="v"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCa8"><a href="#cite_ref-closing_35-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbE">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-closing_35-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbM">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-closing-35" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">A closing quotation mark is added to the beginning of each new paragraph.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-vertical-36" id="cite_note-vertical-36" data-mw-footnote-number="vi"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCbQ"><a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbg">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbo">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-3" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCbs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCbw">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-4" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCb0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCb4">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-5" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCb8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCcA">6</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-6" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCcE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCcI">7</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-vertical_36-7" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCcM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCcQ">8</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-vertical-36" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Only used when text is written vertically (up-to-down and right-to-left).</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-rotated-39" id="cite_note-rotated-39" data-mw-footnote-number="vii"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCcU"><a href="#cite_ref-rotated_39-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCcY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCcc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rotated_39-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCcg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCck">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rotated_39-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCco"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCcs">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-rotated_39-3" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCcw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCc0">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-rotated-39" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Rotated for use in horizontal text; originally written ﹁<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1320" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwCc4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver" id="mwCc8">⋮</span>﹂ and ﹃<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1321" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwCdA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver" id="mwCdE">⋮</span>﹄ in vertical text</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-opening-50" id="cite_note-opening-50" data-mw-footnote-number="viii"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCdI"><a href="#cite_ref-opening_50-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCdM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCdQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-opening_50-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCdU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCdY">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-opening_50-2" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCdc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCdg">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-opening-50" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Within a quotation, the opening quotation mark is repeated at the beginning of each new paragraph.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-native-52" id="cite_note-native-52" data-mw-footnote-number="ix"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCdk"><a href="#cite_ref-native_52-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCdo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCds">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-native_52-1" data-mw-group="lower-roman" id="mwCdw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCd0">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-native-52" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Usage may vary, depending on the native language of the author and publisher.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-dir-v-83" id="cite_note-dir-v-83" data-mw-footnote-number="x"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCd4"><a href="#cite_ref-dir-v_83-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCd8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCeA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-dir-v-83" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Direction of text is vertical.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-88" id="cite_note-88" data-mw-footnote-number="xi"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCeE"><a href="#cite_ref-88" data-mw-group="lower-roman" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCeI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCeM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-88" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">In the scientific works as definitions and in literature</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-89" id="cite_note-89" data-mw-footnote-number="xii"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCeQ"><a href="#cite_ref-89" data-mw-group="lower-roman" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCeU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCeY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-89" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Tertiary quotation mark (very rare) and in the scientific works as definitions</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-handwriting-105" id="cite_note-handwriting-105" data-mw-footnote-number="xiii"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCec"><a href="#cite_ref-handwriting_105-0" data-mw-group="lower-roman" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCeg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCek">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-handwriting-105" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-roman">Handwriting.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1327" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCeo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"group":{"wt":"summary-lang"},"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=ch|In [[Switzerland]] the same style is used for all four national languages.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt1328" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt1327" id="mwCes">
<div class="mw-references-wrap" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt1331" id="mwCew" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:563}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwCe0"><li about="#cite_note-fr-imprimerie_nationale-55" id="cite_note-fr-imprimerie_nationale-55" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCe4"><a href="#cite_ref-fr-imprimerie_nationale_55-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCe8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCfA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-fr-imprimerie_nationale-55" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">According to the French <span title="French-language text" id="mwCfE"><i lang="fr" id="mwCfI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imprimerie_nationale" title="Imprimerie nationale" id="mwCfM">Imprimerie nationale</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" id="mwCfQ"/>. English quotes are more common on the second level.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-fr-nnbsp-56" id="cite_note-fr-nnbsp-56" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCfU"><a href="#cite_ref-fr-nnbsp_56-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCfY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCfc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-fr-nnbsp-56" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">According to French usage in print and the practice of the French <span title="French-language text" id="mwCfg"><i lang="fr" id="mwCfk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imprimerie_nationale" title="Imprimerie nationale" id="mwCfo">Imprimerie nationale</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" id="mwCfs"/>. A rule in the house style guide recommends NBSP, though.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-fr-nbsp-57" id="cite_note-fr-nbsp-57" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCfw"><a href="#cite_ref-fr-nbsp_57-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCf0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCf4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-fr-nbsp-57" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">According to a rule in the house style guide of the French <span title="French-language text" id="mwCf8"><i lang="fr" id="mwCgA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imprimerie_nationale" title="Imprimerie nationale" id="mwCgE">Imprimerie nationale</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" id="mwCgI"/>. Practice in the style guide and elsewhere shows use of NNBSP, though. Also used in word processing, where NBSP is not justifying, though (except in <span class="nowrap" id="mwCgM">Word 2013</span>, according to <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/msoffice/forum/msoffice_word-mso_windows8-mso_2016/nonbreakable-space-justification-in-word-2016/4fa1ad30-004c-454f-9775-a3beaa91c88b" class="external text" id="mwCgQ">this forum thread</a>).</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-fr-usage-60" id="cite_note-fr-usage-60" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwCgU"><a href="#cite_ref-fr-usage_60-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCgY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCgc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-fr-usage-60" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">According to common French usage and the Quebecois <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_québécois_de_la_langue_française" title="Office québécois de la langue française" id="mwCgg">OQLF</a>.<sup about="#mwt571" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwCgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgs">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgw">]</span></span></a></sup> The French <span title="French-language text" id="mwCg0"><i lang="fr" id="mwCg4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imprimerie_nationale" title="Imprimerie nationale" id="mwCg8">Imprimerie nationale</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text" id="mwChA"/> recommends double angle quotes even on the second level.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ch-61" id="cite_note-ch-61" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwChE"><a href="#cite_ref-ch_61-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwChI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwChM">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ch_61-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwChQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwChU">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ch_61-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwChY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwChc">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ch-61" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Switzerland" title="Switzerland" id="mwChg">Switzerland</a> the same style is used for all four national languages.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-el-second_order-65" id="cite_note-el-second_order-65" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwChk"><a href="#cite_ref-el-second_order_65-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCho"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwChs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-el-second_order-65" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Traditional typographical practice.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-km-76" id="cite_note-km-76" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwChw"><a href="#cite_ref-km_76-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwCh0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwCh4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-km-76" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Inferred from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keyboard_layout#Khmer" title="Keyboard layout" id="mwCh8">keyboard layout</a> and <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.selapa.net/khmerfonts/" class="external text" id="mwCiA">fonts</a>.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwCiE" aria-labelledby="Specific_language_features"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Specific_language_features">Specific language features</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Specific language features"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwCiI" aria-labelledby="Bulgarian"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Bulgarian">Bulgarian</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Bulgarian"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCiM">Contemporary Bulgarian employs the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em_dash" title="Em dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCiQ">em dash</a> or the quotation dash (the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Quotation_dash" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCiU">horizontal bar</a>) followed by a space character at the beginning of each direct-speech segment by a different character in order to mark <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Direct_speech" title="Direct speech" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCiY">direct speech</a> in prose and in most journalistic question and answer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interview" title="Interview" id="mwCic">interviews</a>; in such cases, the use of standard quotation marks is left for in-text citations or to mark the names of institutions, companies, and sometimes also brand or model names.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1332" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCig" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"December 2020"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_December_2020" about="#mwt1332"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1332" id="mwCik"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (December 2020)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

<p id="mwCio"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_quotes" title="Air quotes" id="mwCis">Air quotes</a> are also widely used in face-to-face communication in contemporary Bulgarian but usually resemble <code id="mwCiw">" ... "</code> (secondary: <code id="mwCi0">' ... '</code>) unlike written Bulgarian quotation marks.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwCi4" aria-labelledby="Dutch"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Dutch">Dutch</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Dutch"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1333" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCi8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Expand Dutch","href":"./Template:Expand_Dutch"},"params":{"section":{"wt":"yes"},"1":{"wt":"Aanhalingsteken"},"date":{"wt":"September 2013"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1364180890" about="#mwt1334" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Message box/ambox.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><table class="box-Expand_language plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-notice skin-invert-image" role="presentation" about="#mwt1333"><tbody><tr><td class="mbox-image"><div class="mbox-image-div"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Translation_to_english_arrow.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Translation_to_english_arrow.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Translation_to_english_arrow.svg/60px-Translation_to_english_arrow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Translation_to_english_arrow.svg/120px-Translation_to_english_arrow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="icon" data-file-width="60" data-file-height="20" data-file-type="drawing" height="17" width="50" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div></td><td class="mbox-text"><div class="mbox-text-span"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1214851843" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt1335" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Hidden begin/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .hidden-begin{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;padding:5px;border:none;font-size:95%}.mw-parser-output .hidden-title{font-weight:bold;line-height:1.6;text-align:left}.mw-parser-output .hidden-content{text-align:left}@media all and (max-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .hidden-begin{width:auto!important;clear:none!important;float:none!important}}</style></span><div class="hidden-begin mw-collapsible  mw-collapsed " style="   font-size:100%; padding: 0px;"><div class="hidden-title skin-nightmode-reset-color" style="text-align:center;  padding-right: 3em; font-weight: normal; text-align: left">You can help <b>expand this section with text translated from <a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aanhalingsteken" title="nl:Aanhalingsteken" class="extiw">the corresponding article</a> in Dutch</b>. <span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><i><small>(September 2013)</small></i> <small>Click [show] for important translation instructions.</small></div><div class="hidden-content mw-collapsible-content" style="  ">
<ul><li><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://translate.google.com/translate?&amp;u=https%3A%2F%2Fnl.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FAanhalingsteken&amp;sl=nl&amp;tl=en&amp;prev=_t&amp;hl=en" class="external text">View</a> a machine-translated version of the Dutch article.</li>
<li>Machine translation, like <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://deepl.com" class="external text">DeepL</a> or <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://translate.google.com/" class="external text">Google Translate</a>, is a useful starting point for translations, but translators must follow the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:LLM-assisted_translation" title="Wikipedia:LLM-assisted translation">LLM translation guideline</a>, revise errors as necessary and confirm that the translation is accurate, rather than simply copy-pasting machine-translated text into the English Wikipedia.</li>
<li>Consider <b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Expand_Dutch#Topics_and_categorization" title="Template:Expand Dutch">adding a topic</a></b> to this template: there are already 238 articles in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Articles_needing_translation_from_Dutch_Wikipedia" title="Category:Articles needing translation from Dutch Wikipedia">main category</a>, and specifying<code style="display: none;" class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-wikitext mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt1336" id="mwCjA" data-mw='{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"wikitext","inline":"","style":"display: none;"}}'></code><code class="mw-highlight"><span class="p"><span typeof="mw:Entity">|</span></span><span class="nl">topic</span><span class="o">=</span></code> will aid in categorization.</li>
<li>Do not translate text that appears unreliable or low-quality. If possible, verify the text with references provided in the foreign-language article.</li>
<li>You <b>must</b> provide <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Copying_within_Wikipedia" title="Wikipedia:Copying within Wikipedia">copyright attribution</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Edit_summary" title="Help:Edit summary">edit summary</a> accompanying your translation by providing an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Interlanguage_links" title="Help:Interlanguage links">interlanguage link</a> to the source of your translation. A model attribution edit summary is <code>Content in this edit is translated from the existing Dutch Wikipedia article at [[:nl:Aanhalingsteken]]; see its history for attribution.</code></li>
<li>You may also add the template <code>{{Translated|nl|Aanhalingsteken}}</code> to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Quotation_mark" title="Talk:Quotation mark">talk page</a>.</li>
<li>For more guidance, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Translation" title="Wikipedia:Translation">Wikipedia:Translation</a>.</li></ul></div></div></div></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1333"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_needing_translation_from_Dutch_Wikipedia"/></span>
<p id="mwCjE">The standard form in the preceding table is taught in schools and used in handwriting. Most large newspapers have kept these low-high quotation marks, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1337" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCjI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„"}},"i":0}}]}'>„</span> and <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1338" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCjM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"”"}},"i":0}}]}'>”</span>; otherwise, the alternative form with single or double English-style quotes is now often the only form seen in printed matter. Neutral (straight) quotation marks, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1339" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCjQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\""}},"i":0}}]}'>"</span> and <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1340" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCjU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'>'</span>, are used widely, especially in texts typed on computers and on websites.<sup about="#mwt1343" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110"}}'><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwCjY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjg">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCjo">Although not generally common in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netherlands" title="Netherlands" id="mwCjs">Netherlands</a> any more, double angle (guillemet) quotation marks are still sometimes used in Belgium. Examples include the Flemish <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HUMO" title="HUMO" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCjw">HUMO</a> magazine and the Metro newspaper in Brussels.<sup about="#mwt1346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111"}}'><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwCj0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCj4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCj8">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwCkE" aria-labelledby="German"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="German">German</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: German"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCkI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCkM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg/500px-Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg/1280px-Quotation_marks_and_similar_signs.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3284" data-file-height="343" data-file-type="drawing" height="52" width="500" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCkQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCkU">Different forms of German and English quotation marks and similar looking signs</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCkY">The symbol used as the left (typographical) quote in English is used as the right quote in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany" title="Germany" id="mwCkc">Germany</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austria" title="Austria" id="mwCkg">Austria</a> and a "low double comma" <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1347" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCkk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„"}},"i":0}}]}'>„</span> (not used in English) is used for the left quote. Its single quote form <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1348" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCko" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"‚"}},"i":0}}]}'>‚</span> looks like a comma.</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwCks">
<tbody id="mwCkw"><tr id="mwCk0">
<th id="mwCk4">Samples</th><th id="mwCk8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwClA">Unicode</a> (decimal)</th><th id="mwClE">HTML</th><th id="mwClI">Description</th>
<th id="mwClM">Wrong Symbols</th></tr>
<tr id="mwClQ">
<td id="mwClU"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1349" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwClY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|‚{{color|silver|A}}‘}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">‚<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1350" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>‘</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwClc"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1351" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwClg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+201A (8218)"},"2":{"wt":"U+2018 (8216)"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1352" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1351" id="mwClk"><ul><li>U+201A (8218)</li><li>U+2018 (8216)</li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwClo"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1353" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCls" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;sbquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;lsquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1354" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1353" id="mwClw"><ul><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>sbquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>lsquo;</li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwCl0">German single quotes (left and right)</td>
<td id="mwCl4"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1355" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCl8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":", – comma (U + 002C) left"},"2":{"wt":"&apos;  – apostrophe (U+0027) right"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1356" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1355" id="mwCmA"><ul><li>, – comma (U + 002C) left</li><li>'  – apostrophe (U+0027) right</li></ul></div></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCmE">
<td id="mwCmI"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1357" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCmM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|„{{color|silver|A}}“}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">„<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1358" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>“</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCmQ"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1359" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCmU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+201E (8222)"},"2":{"wt":"U+201C (8220)"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1360" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1359" id="mwCmY"><ul><li>U+201E (8222)</li><li>U+201C (8220)</li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwCmc"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1361" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCmg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;bdquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;ldquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1362" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1361" id="mwCmk"><ul><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>bdquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>ldquo;</li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwCmo">German double quotes (left and right)</td>
<td id="mwCms">" – neutral (vertical) double quotes (U+0022)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwCmw">Some fonts, e.g. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdana" title="Verdana" id="mwCm0">Verdana</a>, were not designed with the flexibility to use an English left quote as a German right quote. Such fonts are therefore typographically incompatible with this German usage.</p>

<p id="mwCm4">Double quotes are standard for denoting speech in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_language" title="German language" id="mwCm8">German</a>.</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1363" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCnA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|de|Andreas fragte mich: „Hast du den Artikel ‚EU-Erweiterung‘ gelesen?“}} (Andreas asked me: \"Have you read the &apos;EU Expansion&apos; article?\")"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r996643573" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt1364" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .block-indent{padding-left:3em;padding-right:0;overflow:hidden}</style></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1363" id="mwCnE"><span title="German-language text"><i lang="de">Andreas fragte mich: „Hast du den Artikel ‚EU-Erweiterung‘ gelesen?“</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_German-language_text"/> (Andreas asked me: "Have you read the 'EU Expansion' article?")</div>

<p id="mwCnI">This style of quoting is also used in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulgarian_language" title="Bulgarian language" id="mwCnM">Bulgarian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Czech_language" title="Czech language" id="mwCnQ">Czech</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_language" title="Danish language" id="mwCnU">Danish</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Estonian_language" title="Estonian language" id="mwCnY">Estonian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian_language" title="Georgian language" id="mwCnc">Georgian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_language" title="Icelandic language" id="mwCng">Icelandic</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latvian_language" title="Latvian language" id="mwCnk">Latvian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithuanian_language" title="Lithuanian language" id="mwCno">Lithuanian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_language" title="Russian language" id="mwCns">Russian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbo-Croatian_language" title="Serbo-Croatian language" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCnw">Serbo-Croatian</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovak_language" title="Slovak language" id="mwCn0">Slovak</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovene_language" title="Slovene language" id="mwCn4">Slovene</a> and in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_language" title="Ukrainian language" id="mwCn8">Ukrainian</a>. <span class="cleanup-needed-content" style="padding-left:0.1em; padding-right:0.1em; color:var(--color-subtle, #54595d); border:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle, #c8ccd1);" about="#mwt1365" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCoA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Clarify ","href":"./Template:Clarify"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"In Bulgarian, Icelandic, Estonian, Lithuanian, and Russian, single quotation marks are not used."},"reason":{"wt":"Is this true of the other languages listed above, too? Need citations!"},"date":{"wt":"July 2017"}},"i":0}}]}'>In Bulgarian, Icelandic, Estonian, Lithuanian, and Russian, single quotation marks are not used.</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Wikipedia_articles_needing_clarification_from_July_2017" about="#mwt1365"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="margin-left:0.1em; white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1365" id="mwCoE"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Please_clarify" title="Wikipedia:Please clarify"><span title="Is this true of the other languages listed above, too? Need citations! (July 2017)">clarification needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

<p id="mwCoI">Sometimes, especially in novels, guillemets (angled quotation marks) are used in Germany and Austria (but pointing in the opposite direction compared to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_(language)" title="French (language)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCoM">French</a>): <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1366" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCoQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"»A ›B‹?«"}},"i":0}}]}'>»A ›B‹?«</span></p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1367" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCoU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|de|Andreas fragte mich: »Hast du den Artikel ›EU-Erweiterung‹ gelesen?«}}&lt;br />\nAndreas asked me: \"Have you read the &apos;EU Expansion&apos; article?\""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1368" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1367" id="mwCoY"><span title="German-language text"><i lang="de">Andreas fragte mich: »Hast du den Artikel ›EU-Erweiterung‹ gelesen?«</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_German-language_text"/><br/>
Andreas asked me: "Have you read the 'EU Expansion' article?"</div>

<p id="mwCoc">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Switzerland" title="Switzerland" id="mwCog">Switzerland</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#French" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCok">French-style angle quotation mark sets</a> are also used for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_language" title="German language" id="mwCoo">German</a> printed text: «A ‹B›?»</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1369" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCos" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|de|Andreas fragte mich: «Hast du den Artikel ‹EU-Erweiterung› gelesen?»}}&lt;br />\nAndreas asked me: &apos;Have you read the \"EU Expansion\" article?&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1370" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1369" id="mwCow"><span title="German-language text"><i lang="de">Andreas fragte mich: «Hast du den Artikel ‹EU-Erweiterung› gelesen?»</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_German-language_text"/><br/>
Andreas asked me: 'Have you read the "EU Expansion" article?'</div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwCo0" aria-labelledby="Finnish_and_Swedish"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Finnish_and_Swedish">Finnish and Swedish</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Finnish and Swedish"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwCo4">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_language" title="Finnish language" id="mwCo8">Finnish</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swedish_language" title="Swedish language" id="mwCpA">Swedish</a>, right quotes, called citation marks, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1371" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCpE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"”...”"}},"i":0}}]}'>”...”</span>, are used to mark both the beginning and the end of a quote. Double right-pointing angular quotes, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1372" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCpI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"»...»"}},"i":0}}]}'>»...»</span>, can also be used.</p>

<p id="mwCpM">Alternatively, an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/En-dash" title="En-dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCpQ">en-dash</a> followed by a (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-breaking_space" title="Non-breaking space" id="mwCpU">non-breaking</a>) space can be used to denote the beginning of quoted speech, in which case the end of the quotation is not specifically denoted (see section <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Quotation_dash" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCpY">Quotation dash</a> below). A line-break should not be allowed between the en-dash and the first word of the quotation.</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwCpc">
<tbody id="mwCpg"><tr id="mwCpk">
<th id="mwCpo">Samples</th><th id="mwCps"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwCpw">Unicode</a> (decimal)</th><th id="mwCp0">HTML</th><th id="mwCp4">Description</th></tr>
<tr id="mwCp8">
<td id="mwCqA"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1373" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCqE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|’{{color|silver|A}}’}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">’<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1374" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>’</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCqI">U+2019 (8217)</td>
<td id="mwCqM"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCqQ">&amp;</span>rsquo;</td>
<td id="mwCqU">Secondary level quotation</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCqY">
<td id="mwCqc"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1375" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCqg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|”{{color|silver|A}}”}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">”<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1376" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>”</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCqk">U+201D (8221)</td>
<td id="mwCqo"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCqs">&amp;</span>rdquo;</td>
<td id="mwCqw">Primary level quotation</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCq0">
<td id="mwCq4"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1377" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCq8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|»{{color|silver|A}}»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">»<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1378" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCrA">U+00BB (187)</td>
<td id="mwCrE"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCrI">&amp;</span>raquo;</td>
<td id="mwCrM">Alternative primary level quotation</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCrQ">
<td id="mwCrU"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1379" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCrY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|–&amp;nbsp;{{color|silver|A}}}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">–<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1380" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span></span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCrc">U+2013 (8211)</td>
<td id="mwCrg"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCrk">&amp;</span>ndash;</td>
<td id="mwCro">Alternative denotation at the beginning of quoted speech</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwCrs" aria-labelledby="French"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="French">French</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: French"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1381" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCrw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"uncited section","href":"./Template:Uncited_section"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"March 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1364180890" about="#mwt1382" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Message box/ambox.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><table class="box-Unreferenced_section plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-content ambox-Unreferenced" role="presentation" about="#mwt1381"><tbody><tr><td class="mbox-image"><div class="mbox-image-div"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Question_book-new.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Question_book-new.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/99/Question_book-new.svg/60px-Question_book-new.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/99/Question_book-new.svg/120px-Question_book-new.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="icon" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="399" data-file-type="drawing" height="39" width="50" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div></td><td class="mbox-text"><div class="mbox-text-span">This section <b>does not <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citing_sources" title="Wikipedia:Citing sources">cite</a> any <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability">sources</a></b>.<span class="hide-when-compact"> Please help <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Quotation_mark" title="Special:EditPage/Quotation mark">improve this section</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Referencing_for_beginners" title="Help:Referencing for beginners">adding citations to reliable sources</a>. Unsourced material may be challenged and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Burden_of_evidence" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability">removed</a>.</span>  <span class="date-container"><i>(<span class="date">March 2025</span>)</i></span><span class="hide-when-compact"><i> (<small><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal" title="Help:Maintenance template removal">Learn how and when to remove this message</a></small>)</i></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1381"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_needing_additional_references_from_March_2025"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_needing_additional_references"/></span>

<p id="mwCr0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_language" title="French language" id="mwCr4">French</a> uses angle quotation marks (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillemet" title="Guillemet" id="mwCr8">guillemets</a>, or <i id="mwCsA">duck-foot quotes</i>), adding a 'quarter-em space'<sup about="#mwt1383" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-112" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-112"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{unichar|2005|Four-Per-Em Space|nlink=Space (punctuation)|html=}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-112" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwCsE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCsI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsM">[</span>a<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsQ">]</span></span></a></sup> within the quotes. With proper localization, computers automatically add the proper spacing. When localization is not available, many people use a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-breaking_space" title="Non-breaking space" id="mwCsU">non-breaking space</a> between the quotation mark and the nearest word inside it<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1392" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCsY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_February_2024" about="#mwt1392"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1392" id="mwCsc"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (February 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> because the difference between a non-breaking space and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitespace_character#Unicode" title="Whitespace character" id="mwCsg">four-per-em space</a> is virtually imperceptible, many <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_fonts" title="Computer fonts" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCsk">computer fonts</a> do not include a quarter-em space, and the Unicode quarter-em space is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_wrap_and_word_wrap" title="Line wrap and word wrap" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCso">breakable</a>. Even more commonly, many people put a normal (breaking) space inside the quotation marks<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1393" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCss" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_February_2024" about="#mwt1393"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1393" id="mwCsw"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (February 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> because the non-breaking space cannot be accessed easily from the keyboard, or because they are not aware of this typographical refinement. Using a breakable space of any kind often results in a quotation mark appearing alone at the beginning of a line, since the quotation mark is erroneously treated as an independent word.</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1394" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCs0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|«&amp;nbsp;Voulez-vous un sandwich, Henri&amp;nbsp;?&amp;nbsp;»}}&lt;br />\n“Would you like a sandwich, Henri?”"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1395" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1394" id="mwCs4"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Voulez-vous un sandwich, Henri<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>?<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>»</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
“Would you like a sandwich, Henri?”</div>

<p id="mwCs8">French news sites such as <i id="mwCtA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libération" title="Libération" id="mwCtE">Libération</a></i>, <i id="mwCtI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Échos_(France)" title="Les Échos (France)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCtM">Les Échos</a></i> and <i id="mwCtQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Figaro" title="Le Figaro" id="mwCtU">Le Figaro</a></i> do not add manual spacing, leaving it up to localization and the browser to space the guillemets properly. </p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwCtY">
<tbody id="mwCtc"><tr id="mwCtg">
<th scope="col" rowspan="2" id="mwCtk">Sample</th>
<th scope="col" colspan="2" id="mwCto"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwCts">Unicode</a> (decimal) HTML</th>
<th scope="col" rowspan="2" id="mwCtw">Description</th></tr>
<tr id="mwCt0">
<th scope="col" id="mwCt4">Quote</th>
<th scope="col" id="mwCt8">Space</th></tr>
<tr id="mwCuA">
<td id="mwCuE"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1396" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCuI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|«&amp;nbsp;{{color|silver|A}}&amp;nbsp;»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1397" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td rowspan="3" id="mwCuM"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1398" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCuQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+00AB (171) &apos;&apos;&amp;amp;laquo;&apos;&apos;"},"2":{"wt":"U+00BB (187) &apos;&apos;&amp;amp;raquo;&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1399" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1398" id="mwCuU"><ul><li>U+00AB (171) <i><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>laquo;</i></li><li>U+00BB (187) <i><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>raquo;</i></li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwCuY">U+00A0 (160) <i id="mwCuc"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCug">&amp;</span>nbsp;</i></td>
<td id="mwCuk">French double angle quotes (left and right), legacy (approximative) spacing usual on the web, with <i id="mwCuo">normal</i> (four per em) <i id="mwCus">no-break space</i> (justifying, thus inappropriate)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCuw">
<td id="mwCu0"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1400" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCu4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|«{{thinsp}}{{color|silver|A}}{{thinsp}}»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">«<span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1401" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCu8">U+202F (8239) <i id="mwCvA"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCvE">&amp;</span>#x202F;</i></td>
<td id="mwCvI">French double angle quotes (left and right), correct spacing used by typographers, with <i id="mwCvM">narrow</i> (six per em) non-breaking spaces, represented on the web using <i id="mwCvQ">narrow no-break space</i></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCvU">
<td id="mwCvY"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1402" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCvc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|«{{color|silver|A}}»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">«<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1403" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCvg"></td>
<td id="mwCvk">French double angle quotes (left and right) without space (not recommended in French)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCvo">
<td id="mwCvs"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1404" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCvw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|‹&amp;nbsp;{{color|silver|A}}&amp;nbsp;›}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">‹<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1405" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>›</span></span></span></span></td>
<td rowspan="3" id="mwCv0"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1406" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCv4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Unbulleted list","href":"./Template:Unbulleted_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+2039 (8249) &apos;&apos;&amp;amp;lsaquo;&apos;&apos;"},"2":{"wt":"U+203A (8250) &apos;&apos;&amp;amp;rsaquo;&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1407" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="plainlist" about="#mwt1406" id="mwCv8"><ul><li>U+2039 (8249) <i><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>lsaquo;</i></li><li>U+203A (8250) <i><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>rsaquo;</i></li></ul></div></td>
<td id="mwCwA">U+00A0 (160) <i id="mwCwE"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCwI">&amp;</span>nbsp;</i></td>
<td id="mwCwM">French single angle quotes (left and right), alternate form for embedded quotations, legacy (approximative) spacing usual on the web, with <i id="mwCwQ">normal</i> (four per em) <i id="mwCwU">no-break space</i> (justifying, thus inappropriate)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCwY">
<td id="mwCwc"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1408" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCwg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|‹{{thinsp}}{{color|silver|A}}{{thinsp}}›}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">‹<span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1409" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span>›</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCwk">U+202F (8239) <i id="mwCwo"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCws">&amp;</span>#x202F;</i></td>
<td id="mwCww">French single angle quotes (left and right), alternate form for embedded quotations, correct spacing used by typographers, with <i id="mwCw0">narrow</i> (six per em) non-breaking spaces, represented on the web using <i id="mwCw4">narrow no-break space</i></td></tr>
<tr id="mwCw8">
<td id="mwCxA"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1410" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCxE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|‹{{color|silver|A}}›}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">‹<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1411" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>›</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwCxI"></td>
<td id="mwCxM">French single angle quotes (left and right) without space (not recommended in French)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCxQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Guillemets_(Imprimerie_nationale,_1934).png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCxU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Guillemets_(Imprimerie_nationale,_1934).png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Guillemets_%28Imprimerie_nationale%2C_1934%29.png/250px-Guillemets_%28Imprimerie_nationale%2C_1934%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/Guillemets_%28Imprimerie_nationale%2C_1934%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x" data-file-width="368" data-file-height="82" data-file-type="bitmap" height="56" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCxY"/></a><figcaption id="mwCxc">Guillemets by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imprimerie_nationale" title="Imprimerie nationale" id="mwCxg">Imprimerie nationale</a> in <i id="mwCxk">Bulletin de l’Agence générale des colonies</i>, No. 302, Mai 1934, showing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comma" title="Comma" id="mwCxo">comma</a>-shaped symbols sitting on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baseline_(typography)" title="Baseline (typography)" id="mwCxs">baseline</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCxw">Initially, the French guillemets were not angle shaped but also used the comma (6/9) shape.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1412" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCx0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_August_2024" about="#mwt1412"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1412" id="mwCx4"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> They were different from English quotes because they were standing (like today's guillemets) <i id="mwCx8">on</i> the baseline (like lowercase letters), not raised above it (like apostrophes and English quotation marks) or hanging below it (like commas). At the beginning of the nineteenth century, this shape evolved to look like <small id="mwCyA"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1413" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCyE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"(("}},"i":0}}]}'>((</span></small><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCyI"> </span>small parentheses<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCyM"> </span><small id="mwCyQ"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1414" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCyU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"))"}},"i":0}}]}'>))</span></small>. The angle shape was introduced later to make them easier to distinguish from apostrophes, commas and parentheses in handwritten manuscripts submitted to publishers. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwCyY">Unicode</a> currently does not provide alternate codes for these 6/9 guillemets on the baseline, as they are considered to be form variants of guillemets, implemented in older French typography (such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Didot_(typeface)" title="Didot (typeface)" id="mwCyc">Didot font</a> design). With this older style there was also not necessarily any distinction of shape between the opening and closing guillemets; both often pointed to the right (as today's French closing guillemets do).<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1415" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCyg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_August_2024" about="#mwt1415"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1415" id="mwCyk"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

<p id="mwCyo">In old-style printed books, when quotations span multiple lines of text (including multiple paragraphs), an additional closing quotation sign is traditionally used at the <i id="mwCys">beginning</i> of each line continuing a quotation; this right-pointing guillemet at the beginning of a line does <b id="mwCyw">not</b> close the current quotation. This convention was consistently used from the beginning of the 19th century by most book printers, but is no longer in use today. Such insertion of continuation quotation marks was rigidly maintained, even at a word hyphenation break. Since these continuation marks are obsolete in French, there is no support for automatic insertion of continuation guillemets in HTML or CSS, nor in word-processors. Old-style typesetting is emulated by breaking up the final layout with manual line breaks, and inserting the quotation marks at line start, much like angle brackets before quoted plain text e-mail:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1416" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCy0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|« C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais, soutient&lt;br />» le ministre. Ces investissements stimuleront la crois-&lt;br />» sance économique. »}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1417" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1416" id="mwCy4"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais, soutient<br/>» le ministre. Ces investissements stimuleront la crois-<br/>» sance économique.<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>»</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/></div>

<p id="mwCy8">Unlike English, French does not identify unquoted material within a quotation by using a second set of quotation marks. Compare:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1418" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|« C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais, soutient le ministre. Ces investissements stimuleront la croissance économique. »|italic=set}}&lt;br />\n\"This is a great day for Montrealers\", the minister maintained. \"These investments will stimulate economic growth.\""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1419" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1418" id="mwCzE"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais, soutient le ministre. Ces investissements stimuleront la croissance économique.<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>»</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
"This is a great day for Montrealers", the minister maintained. "These investments will stimulate economic growth."</div>

<p id="mwCzI">For clarity, some newspapers put nested quoted material in italics:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1420" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|« &apos;&apos;C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais,&apos;&apos; soutient le ministre. &apos;&apos;Ces investissements stimuleront la croissance économique.&apos;&apos; »|italic=unset}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1421" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1420" id="mwCzQ"><span title="French-language text"><span lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span><i>C’est une belle journée pour les Montréalais,</i> soutient le ministre. <i>Ces investissements stimuleront la croissance économique.</i><span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>»</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/></div>

<p id="mwCzU">The French Imprimerie nationale (cf. <i id="mwCzY">Lexique des règles typographiques en usage à l'Imprimerie nationale</i>, presses de l'Imprimerie nationale, Paris, 2002) does not use different quotation marks for nesting quotes:</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1422" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|«&amp;nbsp;Son «&amp;nbsp;explication&amp;nbsp;» n’est qu’un mensonge&amp;nbsp;», s’indigna le député.}}&lt;br />\n\"His &apos;explanation&apos; is just a lie\", the deputy protested."}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1423" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1422" id="mwCzg"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Son «<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>explication<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>» n’est qu’un mensonge<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>», s’indigna le député.</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
"His 'explanation' is just a lie", the deputy protested.</div>

<p id="mwCzk">In this case, when there should be two adjacent opening or closing marks, only one is written:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1424" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|Il répondit&amp;nbsp;: «&amp;nbsp;Ce n’est qu’un «&amp;nbsp;gadget&amp;nbsp;!&amp;nbsp;».}}&lt;br />\nHe answered: \"It&apos;s only a &apos;gizmo&apos;.\""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1425" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1424" id="mwCzs"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">Il répondit<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>: «<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Ce n’est qu’un «<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>gadget<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>!<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>».</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
He answered: "It's only a 'gizmo'."</div>

<p id="mwCzw">The use of English quotation marks is increasing in French and usually follows English rules, for instance in situations when the keyboard or the software context doesn't allow the use of guillemets. The French news site <i id="mwCz0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L'Humanité" title="L'Humanité" id="mwCz4">L'Humanité</a></i> uses straight quotation marks along with angle ones.</p>

<p id="mwCz8">English quotes are also used sometimes for nested quotations:</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1426" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC0A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|«&amp;nbsp;Son “explication” n’est qu’un mensonge&amp;nbsp;», s’indigna le député.}}&lt;br />\n\"His &apos;explanation&apos; is just a lie\", the deputy protested."}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1427" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1426" id="mwC0E"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Son “explication” n’est qu’un mensonge<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>», s’indigna le député.</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
"His 'explanation' is just a lie", the deputy protested.</div>

<p id="mwC0I">But the most frequent convention used in printed books for nested quotations is to style them in italics. Single quotation marks are much more rarely used, and multiple levels of quotations using the same marks is often considered confusing for readers:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1428" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC0M" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|«&amp;nbsp;Son &apos;&apos;explication&apos;&apos; n’est qu’un mensonge&amp;nbsp;», s’indigna le député.|italic=unset}}&lt;br />\n{{lang|fr|Il répondit&amp;nbsp;: «&amp;nbsp;Ce n’est qu’un &apos;&apos;gadget&apos;&apos;&amp;nbsp;!&amp;nbsp;».|italic=unset}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1429" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1428" id="mwC0Q"><span title="French-language text"><span lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Son <i>explication</i> n’est qu’un mensonge<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>», s’indigna le député.</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
<span title="French-language text"><span lang="fr">Il répondit<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>: «<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Ce n’est qu’un <i>gadget</i><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>!<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>».</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/></div>

<p id="mwC0U">Further, running dialogue does not use quotation marks beyond the first sentence, as changes in speaker are indicated by a dash, as opposed to the English use of closing and re-opening the quotation. (For other languages employing dashes, see section <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Quotation_dash" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwC0Y">Quotation dash</a> below.) The dashes may be used entirely without quotation marks as well. In general, quotation marks are extended to encompass as much speech as possible, including not just unspoken text such as "he said" (as previously noted), but also as long as the conversion extends. The quotation marks end at the last word of spoken text (rather than extending to the end of the paragraph) when the final part is not spoken.</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1430" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC0c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|fr|«&amp;nbsp;Je ne vous parle pas, monsieur, dit-il.}}&lt;br />\n{{lang|fr|—&amp;nbsp;Mais je vous parle, moi&amp;nbsp;!&amp;nbsp;» s’écria le jeune homme exaspéré de ce mélange d’insolence et de bonnes manières, de convenance et de dédain.}} ([[Alexandre Dumas, père|Dumas]], &apos;&apos;[[The Three Musketeers|Les trois mousquetaires]]&apos;&apos;)\n\n\"I am not speaking to you, sir\", he said.&lt;br />\n\"But &apos;&apos;I&apos;&apos; am speaking to you!\" cried the young man, exasperated by this combination of insolence and good manners, of protocol and disdain."}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1431" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1430" id="mwC0g"><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">«<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Je ne vous parle pas, monsieur, dit-il.</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/><br/>
<p><span title="French-language text"><i lang="fr">—<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Mais je vous parle, moi<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>!<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>» s’écria le jeune homme exaspéré de ce mélange d’insolence et de bonnes manières, de convenance et de dédain.</i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_French-language_text"/> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandre_Dumas,_père" title="Alexandre Dumas, père" class="mw-redirect">Dumas</a>, <i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Three_Musketeers" title="The Three Musketeers">Les trois mousquetaires</a></i>)</p>

<p>"I am not speaking to you, sir", he said.<br/></p>
"But <i>I</i> am speaking to you!" cried the young man, exasperated by this combination of insolence and good manners, of protocol and disdain.</div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwC0k" aria-labelledby="Greek"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Greek">Greek</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Greek"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwC0o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_language" title="Greek language" id="mwC0s">Greek</a> uses angled quotation marks (<b id="mwC0w"><span title="Greek-language text" about="#mwt1432" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC00" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"el"},"2":{"wt":"[[wikt:εισαγωγικά|εισαγωγικά]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="el"><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/εισαγωγικά" title="wikt:εισαγωγικά" class="extiw">εισαγωγικά</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text" about="#mwt1432" id="mwC04"/></b> – <i id="mwC08">isagogiká</i>):</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1433" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC1A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|el|«Μιλάει σοβαρά;» ρώτησε την Μαρία.&lt;br />«Ναι, σίγουρα», αποκρίθηκε.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1434" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1433" id="mwC1E"><span title="Greek-language text"><span lang="el">«Μιλάει σοβαρά;» ρώτησε την Μαρία.<br/>«Ναι, σίγουρα», αποκρίθηκε.</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text"/></div>
<p id="mwC1I">and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Quotation_dash" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwC1M">quotation dash</a> (<b id="mwC1Q"><span title="Greek-language text" about="#mwt1435" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC1U" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"el"},"2":{"wt":"[[wikt:παύλα|παύλα]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="el"><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/παύλα" title="wikt:παύλα" class="extiw">παύλα</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text" about="#mwt1435" id="mwC1Y"/></b> – <i id="mwC1c">pávla</i>):</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1436" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC1g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|el|― Μιλάει σοβαρά; ρώτησε την Μαρία.&lt;br />― Ναι, σίγουρα, αποκρίθηκε.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1437" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1436" id="mwC1k"><span title="Greek-language text"><span lang="el">― Μιλάει σοβαρά; ρώτησε την Μαρία.<br/>― Ναι, σίγουρα, αποκρίθηκε.</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text"/></div>
<p id="mwC1o">which translate to:</p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1438" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC1s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Is he serious?\" he asked Maria.&lt;br />\n\"Yes, certainly,\" she replied."}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1439" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1438" id="mwC1w">"Is he serious?" he asked Maria.<br/>
"Yes, certainly," she replied.</div>
<p id="mwC10">A closing quotation mark, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1440" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC14" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"»"}},"i":0}}]}'>»</span>, is added to the beginning of each new paragraph within a quotation.</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1441" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC18" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{lang|el|« Η Βικιπαίδεια ή Wikipedia είναι ένα συλλογικό εγκυκλοπαιδικό&lt;br />» εγχείρημα που έχει συσταθεί στο Διαδίκτυο, παγκόσμιο, πολύγλωσσο,&lt;br />» που λειτουργεί με την αρχή του wiki. »}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1442" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1441" id="mwC2A"><span title="Greek-language text"><span lang="el">«<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>Η Βικιπαίδεια ή Wikipedia είναι ένα συλλογικό εγκυκλοπαιδικό<br/>» εγχείρημα που έχει συσταθεί στο Διαδίκτυο, παγκόσμιο, πολύγλωσσο,<br/>» που λειτουργεί με την αρχή του wiki.<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace"> </span>»</span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text"/></div>

<p id="mwC2E">When quotations are nested, the nested parts use English-style quotation marks, double and then (if necessary) single: <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1443" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC2I" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"«...“...‘...’...”...»"}},"i":0}}]}'>«...“...‘...’...”...»</span>.<sup about="#mwt1444" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-el-2_67-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"el-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-el-2-67" id="mwC2M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2U">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwC2c">
<tbody id="mwC2g"><tr id="mwC2k">
<th id="mwC2o">Samples</th><th id="mwC2s"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwC2w">Unicode</a> (decimal)</th><th id="mwC20">HTML</th><th id="mwC24">Description</th></tr>
<tr id="mwC28">
<td id="mwC3A"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1445" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC3E" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|«{{color|silver|Α}}»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">«<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1446" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">Α</span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC3I"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1367478826" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1447" id="mwC3M" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+00AB (0171)"},"2":{"wt":"U+00BB (0187)"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output ul.cslist,.mw-parser-output ul.sslist,.mw-parser-output ul.andlist,.mw-parser-output ul.andlistoxford{margin:0;padding:0;display:inline-block;list-style:none}.mw-parser-output ul.cslist-embedded{display:inline}.mw-parser-output .cslist li,.mw-parser-output .sslist li,.mw-parser-output .andlist li,.mw-parser-output .andlistoxford li{margin:0;padding:0 0.25em 0 0;display:inline-block}.mw-parser-output .cslist li:after,.mw-parser-output .andlistoxford li:after{content:", "}.mw-parser-output .sslist li:after{content:"; "}.mw-parser-output .cslist li:last-child:after,.mw-parser-output .sslist li:last-child:after,.mw-parser-output .andlist li:last-child:after,.mw-parser-output .andlistoxford li:last-child:after{content:none}.mw-parser-output .andlist li:nth-last-child(2):after{content:" and "}.mw-parser-output .andlistoxford li:nth-last-child(2):after{content:", and "}</style><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1447" id="mwC3Q"><li>U+00AB (0171)</li><li>U+00BB (0187)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC3U"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1449" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC3Y" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;laquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;raquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1449" id="mwC3c"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>laquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>raquo;</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC3g">Greek first level double quotes (<b id="mwC3k"><span title="Greek-language text" about="#mwt1451" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC3o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"el"},"2":{"wt":"[[wikt:εισαγωγικά|εισαγωγικά]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><span lang="el"><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/εισαγωγικά" title="wikt:εισαγωγικά" class="extiw">εισαγωγικά</a></span></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Greek-language_text" about="#mwt1451" id="mwC3s"/></b>)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwC3w">
<td id="mwC30"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1452" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC34" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|―&amp;nbsp;{{color|silver|Α}}}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">―<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1453" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">Α</span></span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC38">U+2014 (8212)</td>
<td id="mwC4A"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC4E">&amp;</span>mdash;</td>
<td id="mwC4I">Greek direct quotation em-dash</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwC4M" aria-labelledby="Hungarian"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hungarian">Hungarian</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Hungarian"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC4Q">According to current recommendation by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungarian_Academy_of_Sciences" title="Hungarian Academy of Sciences" id="mwC4U">Hungarian Academy of Sciences</a> the main Hungarian quotation marks are comma-shaped double quotation marks set on the base-line at the beginning of the quote and at apostrophe-height at the end of it for first level, (<span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1454" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC4Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„Quote”"}},"i":0}}]}'>„Quote”</span>), reversed »French quotes« without space (the German tradition) for the second level, and thus the following nested quotation pattern emerges:</p>
<ul id="mwC4c"><li id="mwC4g"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1455" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC4k" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„Quote »inside« quote”"}},"i":0}}]}'>„Quote »inside« quote”</span></li></ul>

<p id="mwC4o">... and with third level:</p>
<ul id="mwC4s"><li id="mwC4w"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1456" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC40" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„Quote »inside ’inside of inside’ inside« quote”"}},"i":0}}]}'>„Quote »inside ’inside of inside’ inside« quote”</span></li></ul>

<p id="mwC44">In Hungarian linguistic tradition the meaning of a word is signified by <i id="mwC48">uniform (unpaired)</i> apostrophe-shaped quotation marks:</p>
<ul id="mwC5A"><li id="mwC5E"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1457" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC5I" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;die Biene&apos;&apos; ’méh’"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>die Biene</i> ’méh’</span></li></ul>

<p id="mwC5M">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Quotation_dash" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwC5Q">quotation dash</a> is also used, and is predominant in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belletristic" title="Belletristic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC5U">belletristic</a> literature.</p>
<ul id="mwC5Y"><li id="mwC5c"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1458" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC5g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"– Merre jártál? – kérdezte a köpcös"}},"i":0}}]}'>– Merre jártál? – kérdezte a köpcös</span>.</li></ul>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwC5k">
<tbody id="mwC5o"><tr id="mwC5s">
<th id="mwC5w">Samples</th><th id="mwC50"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwC54">Unicode</a> (decimal)</th><th id="mwC58">HTML</th><th id="mwC6A">Description</th></tr>
<tr id="mwC6E">
<td id="mwC6I"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1459" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC6M" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|„{{color|silver|A}}”}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">„<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1460" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>”</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC6Q"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1461" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC6U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+201E (8222)"},"2":{"wt":"U+201D (8221)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1461" id="mwC6Y"><li>U+201E (8222)</li><li>U+201D (8221)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC6c"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1463" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC6g" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;bdquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;rdquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1463" id="mwC6k"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>bdquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>rdquo;</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC6o">Hungarian first level double quotes (left and right)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwC6s">
<td id="mwC6w"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1465" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC60" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|»{{color|silver|A}}«}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">»<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1466" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>«</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC64"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1467" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC68" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+00BB (0171)"},"2":{"wt":"U+00AB (0187)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1467" id="mwC7A"><li>U+00BB (0171)</li><li>U+00AB (0187)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC7E"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1469" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC7I" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;raquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;laquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1469" id="mwC7M"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>raquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>laquo;</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC7Q">Hungarian second level double quotes (left and right)</td></tr>
<tr id="mwC7U">
<td id="mwC7Y"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1471" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC7c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|’{{color|silver|A}}’}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">’<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1472" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">A</span>’</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC7g">U+2019 (8217)</td>
<td id="mwC7k"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC7o">&amp;</span>rsquo;</td>
<td id="mwC7s">Hungarian <i id="mwC7w">unpaired</i> quotes signifying "meaning of the preceding term"</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwC70" aria-labelledby="Hebrew"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hebrew">Hebrew</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Hebrew"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC74">In Israel, the traditional practice in printing and handwriting is to use „low-high” quote marks.<sup about="#mwt1474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-he-1_69-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"he-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-he-1-69" id="mwC78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8E">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8I">]</span></span></a></sup> Since the 2000s, the plain quotes have become more common.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1473" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC8M" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"September 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_September_2024" about="#mwt1473"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1473" id="mwC8Q"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (September 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> The 2013 revision of the SI-1452 standard for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebrew_keyboard" title="Hebrew keyboard" id="mwC8U">Hebrew keyboard</a>, available since 2012 in Windows 8 and in desktop Linux systems, supports both systems, as does the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gboard" title="Gboard" id="mwC8Y">Gboard</a> keyboard for touchscreen devices.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwC8c" aria-labelledby="Norwegian"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Norwegian">Norwegian</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Norwegian"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC8g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norwegian_language" title="Norwegian language" id="mwC8k">Norwegian</a> uses angled quotation marks (<b id="mwC8o"><span title="Bokmål-language text" about="#mwt1475" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC8s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"lang","href":"./Template:Lang"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"nb"},"2":{"wt":"[[wikt:Anførselstegn|Anførselstegn]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><i lang="nb"><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Anførselstegn" title="wikt:Anførselstegn" class="extiw">Anførselstegn</a></i></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Bokmål-language_text" about="#mwt1475" id="mwC8w"/></b>)</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwC80">
<tbody id="mwC84"><tr id="mwC88">
<th id="mwC9A">Samples</th><th id="mwC9E"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwC9I">Unicode</a> (decimal)</th><th id="mwC9M">HTML</th><th id="mwC9Q">Description</th></tr>
<tr id="mwC9U">
<td id="mwC9Y"><span class="serif-fonts" style="font-family: 'Georgia Pro', Georgia, 'DejaVu Serif', Times, 'Times New Roman', FreeSerif, 'DejaVu Math TeX', 'URW Bookman L', serif; " about="#mwt1476" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC9c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"serif","href":"./Template:Serif"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{huge|«{{color|silver|Α}}»}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;"><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">«<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1477" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">Α</span>»</span></span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC9g"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1478" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC9k" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+00AB (0171)"},"2":{"wt":"U+00BB (0187)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1478" id="mwC9o"><li>U+00AB (0171)</li><li>U+00BB (0187)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwC9s"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1480" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC9w" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;laquo;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;raquo;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1480" id="mwC90"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>laquo;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>raquo;</li></ul></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwC94" aria-labelledby="Polish"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Polish">Polish</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Polish"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1482" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC98" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Update","href":"./Template:Update"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"section"},"reason":{"wt":"The PN-83/P-55366 standard was withdrawn in 2014, according to [[Polish Wikipedia]]"},"inaccurate":{"wt":"yes"},"date":{"wt":"March 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1364180890" about="#mwt1483" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Message box/ambox.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><table class="box-Update plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-content ambox-Update" role="presentation" about="#mwt1482"><tbody><tr><td class="mbox-image"><div class="mbox-image-div"><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Ambox_current_red_Asia_Australia.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Ambox_current_red_Asia_Australia.svg/60px-Ambox_current_red_Asia_Australia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Ambox_current_red_Asia_Australia.svg/120px-Ambox_current_red_Asia_Australia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="" data-file-width="360" data-file-height="290" data-file-type="drawing" height="34" width="42" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span></div></td><td class="mbox-text"><div class="mbox-text-span">This section's <b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Accuracy_dispute" title="Wikipedia:Accuracy dispute">factual accuracy</a> may be compromised due to out-of-date information</b>. The reason given is: <b>The PN-83/P-55366 standard was withdrawn in 2014, according to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polish_Wikipedia" title="Polish Wikipedia">Polish Wikipedia</a></b>.<span class="hide-when-compact"> Please help update this article to reflect recent events or newly available information.</span>  <span class="date-container"><i>(<span class="date">March 2024</span>)</i></span></div></td></tr></tbody></table><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1482"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_obsolete_information_from_March_2024"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_Wikipedia_articles_in_need_of_updating"/></span>
<p id="mwC-A">According to current <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PN-83/P-55366?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="PN-83/P-55366 (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwC-E" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["PN-83/P-55366"]}}'>PN-83/P-55366</a> standard from 1983 (but not dictionaries, see below), <i id="mwC-I">Typesetting rules for composing Polish text</i> (<i id="mwC-M">Zasady składania tekstów w języku polskim</i>) one can use either „ordinary Polish quotes” or «French quotes» (without space) for first level, and ‚single Polish quotes’ or «French quotes» for second level, which gives three styles of nested quotes:</p>

<ol id="mwC-Q"><li id="mwC-U"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1484" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC-Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„Quote ‚inside’ quote”"}},"i":0}}]}'>„Quote ‚inside’ quote”</span></li>
<li id="mwC-c"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1485" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC-g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"„Quote «inside» quote”"}},"i":0}}]}'>„Quote «inside» quote”</span></li>
<li id="mwC-k"><span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1486" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC-o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"«Quote ‚inside’ quote»"}},"i":0}}]}'>«Quote ‚inside’ quote»</span></li></ol>

<p id="mwC-s">There is no space on the internal side of quote marks, with the exception of <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1154941027" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1487" id="mwC-w" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Fraction/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"fraction","href":"./Template:Fraction"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1"},"2":{"wt":"4"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .frac{white-space:nowrap}.mw-parser-output .frac .num,.mw-parser-output .frac .den{font-size:80%;line-height:0;vertical-align:super}.mw-parser-output .frac .den{vertical-align:sub}.mw-parser-output .sr-only{border:0;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:polygon(0px 0px,0px 0px,0px 0px);height:1px;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;padding:0;position:absolute;width:1px}</style><span class="frac" about="#mwt1487" id="mwC-0"><span class="num">1</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">⁄</span><span class="den">4</span></span> <i id="mwC-4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em_(typography)#Firet" title="Em (typography)" id="mwC-8">firet</a></i> (≈ <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1154941027" about="#mwt1489" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC_A" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Fraction/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"fraction","href":"./Template:Fraction"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1"},"2":{"wt":"4"}},"i":0}}]}'/><span class="frac" about="#mwt1489" id="mwC_E"><span class="num">1</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">⁄</span><span class="den">4</span></span> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em_(typography)" title="Em (typography)" id="mwC_I">em</a>) space between two quotation marks when there are no other characters between them (e.g. <span style="font-family:serif; padding-right:0.25em" id="mwC_M">,</span>„ and <span style="font-family:serif; padding-right:0.25em" id="mwC_Q">’</span>”).</p>

<p id="mwC_U">The above rules have not changed since at least the previous <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BN-76/7440-02?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="BN-76/7440-02 (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwC_Y" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["BN-76/7440-02"]}}'>BN-76/7440-02</a> standard from 1976 and are probably much older.</p>
<!-- date and reference to the oldest standard needed -->

<p id="mwC_c">These rules on the use of guillemets conflict with the ones given by Polish dictionaries, including the <i id="mwC_g">Wielki Słownik Ortograficzny PWN</i> recommended by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polish_Language_Council" title="Polish Language Council" id="mwC_k">Polish Language Council</a>. The PWN rules state:</p>

<style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1244412712" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1491" id="mwC_o" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Blockquote/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Blockquote","href":"./Template:Blockquote"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"In specific uses, guillemets also appear. Guillemet marks pointing inwards are used for highlights and in case a quotation occurs inside a quotation. Guillemet marks pointing outwards are used for definitions (mainly in scientific publications and dictionaries), as well as for enclosing spoken lines and indirect speech, especially in poetic texts.&lt;ref>{{cite web |title=Zasady pisowni i interpunkcji |language=pl |url= http://so.pwn.pl/zasady.php?id=629866 |work=Wielki Słownik Ortograficzny (online edition) |publisher=Wydawnictwo Naukowe PWN SA |access-date=11 September 2012 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20121120220728/http://so.pwn.pl/zasady.php?id=629866 |archive-date=20 November 2012}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}}</style><blockquote class="templatequote " about="#mwt1491" id="mwC_s"><p>In specific uses, guillemets also appear. Guillemet marks pointing inwards are used for highlights and in case a quotation occurs inside a quotation. Guillemet marks pointing outwards are used for definitions (mainly in scientific publications and dictionaries), as well as for enclosing spoken lines and indirect speech, especially in poetic texts.<sup about="#mwt1495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwC_w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_4">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_8">]</span></span></a></sup></p></blockquote>

<p id="mwDAA">In Polish printed books and publications, this dictionary-recommended style for guillemets (also known as »German quotes«) is used almost exclusively. In addition to being standard for second level quotes, guillemet quotes are sometimes used as first level quotes in headings and titles, but almost never for ordinary text in paragraphs.</p>

<p id="mwDAE">Another style of quoting is to use an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em-dash" title="Em-dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDAI">em-dash</a> to open a quote; this is used almost exclusively for quoting dialogues rather than for single statements, and is virtually always the one used for that purpose in works of fiction.</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1498" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDAM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Mag skłonił się. Biały kot śpiący obok paleniska ocknął się nagle i spojrzał na niego badawczo.&lt;br />\n— Jak się nazywa ta wieś, panie? — zapytał przybysz. Kowal wzruszył ramionami.&lt;br />\n— Głupi Osioł.&lt;br />\n— Głupi...?&lt;br />\n— Osioł — powtórzył kowal takim tonem, jakby wyzywał gościa, żeby spróbował sobie z niego zażartować. Mag zamyślił się.&lt;br />\n— Ta nazwa ma pewnie swoją historię — stwierdził w końcu. — W innych okolicznościach chętnie bym jej wysłuchał. Ale chciałbym porozmawiać z tobą, kowalu, o twoim synu.\n\nThe wizard bowed. A white cat that had been sleeping by the furnace woke up and watched him carefully.&lt;br />\n“What is the name of this place, sir?” said the wizard.&lt;br />\nThe blacksmith shrugged.&lt;br />\n“Stupid Donkey,” he said. [original English version is \"Bad Ass\", but that&apos;s not a common phrase in Polish]&lt;br />\n“Stupid—?”&lt;br />\n“Donkey,” repeated the blacksmith, his tone defying anyone to make something of it.&lt;br />\nThe wizard considered this.&lt;br />\n“A name with a story behind it,” he said at last, “which were circumstances otherwise I would be pleased to hear. But I would like to speak to you, smith, about your son.”&lt;br />\n(—&amp;thinsp;[[Terry Pratchett]], &apos;&apos;Equal Rites&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1499" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1498" id="mwDAQ">Mag skłonił się. Biały kot śpiący obok paleniska ocknął się nagle i spojrzał na niego badawczo.<br/>
<p>— Jak się nazywa ta wieś, panie? — zapytał przybysz. Kowal wzruszył ramionami.<br/>
— Głupi Osioł.<br/>
— Głupi...?<br/>
— Osioł — powtórzył kowal takim tonem, jakby wyzywał gościa, żeby spróbował sobie z niego zażartować. Mag zamyślił się.<br/>
— Ta nazwa ma pewnie swoją historię — stwierdził w końcu. — W innych okolicznościach chętnie bym jej wysłuchał. Ale chciałbym porozmawiać z tobą, kowalu, o twoim synu.</p>

<p>The wizard bowed. A white cat that had been sleeping by the furnace woke up and watched him carefully.<br/>
“What is the name of this place, sir?” said the wizard.<br/>
The blacksmith shrugged.<br/>
“Stupid Donkey,” he said. [original English version is "Bad Ass", but that's not a common phrase in Polish]<br/>
“Stupid—?”<br/>
“Donkey,” repeated the blacksmith, his tone defying anyone to make something of it.<br/>
The wizard considered this.<br/>
“A name with a story behind it,” he said at last, “which were circumstances otherwise I would be pleased to hear. But I would like to speak to you, smith, about your son.”<br/></p>
(—<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terry_Pratchett" title="Terry Pratchett">Terry Pratchett</a>, <i>Equal Rites</i>)</div>

<p id="mwDAU">An <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/En-dash" title="En-dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDAY">en-dash</a> is sometimes used in place of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em-dash" title="Em-dash" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDAc">em-dash</a>, especially so in newspaper texts.</p>

<table class="wikitable" id="mwDAg">
<tbody id="mwDAk"><tr id="mwDAo">
