<td id="mwDUU"><span style="vertical-align:sub;" about="#mwt1629" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"huge","href":"./Template:Huge"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"《{{color|silver|한}}》"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">《<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1630" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">한</span>》</span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwDUc"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1631" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+300A (12298)"},"2":{"wt":"U+300B (12299)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1631" id="mwDUk"><li>U+300A (12298)</li><li>U+300B (12299)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwDUo"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1633" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUs" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;#x300A;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;#x300B;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1633" id="mwDUw"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>#x300A;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>#x300B;</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwDU0">Double angle brackets<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1635" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDU4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"plainlist","href":"./Template:Plainlist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n* Korean: 겹화살괄호 (&apos;&apos;gyeophwasalgwalho&apos;&apos;)\n* Chinese: 書名號 (&apos;&apos;shū míng hào&apos;&apos;)\n"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1636" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="plainlist " about="#mwt1635" id="mwDU8">
<ul><li>Korean: 겹화살괄호 (<i>gyeophwasalgwalho</i>)</li>
<li>Chinese: 書名號 (<i>shū míng hào</i>)</li></ul>

</div></td>
<td id="mwDVA"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1637" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"plainlist","href":"./Template:Plainlist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n* Korean (titles of newspapers, magazines, periodicals)\n* [[Chinese language|Chinese]] (used for titles of books, documents, movies, pieces of art or music, magazines, newspapers, laws, etc. )\n"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1638" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="plainlist " about="#mwt1637" id="mwDVI">
<ul><li>Korean (titles of newspapers, magazines, periodicals)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_language" title="Chinese language">Chinese</a> (used for titles of books, documents, movies, pieces of art or music, magazines, newspapers, laws, etc. )</li></ul>

</div></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDVM">
<td id="mwDVQ"><span style="vertical-align:sub;" about="#mwt1639" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"huge","href":"./Template:Huge"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"〈{{color|silver|한}}〉"}},"i":0}}]}'><span style="vertical-align:sub;line-height:180%"><span style="font-size:180%; vertical-align:sub;">〈<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239334494" about="#mwt1640" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Color/styles.css"}}'/><span class="tmp-color" style="color:silver">한</span>〉</span></span></span></td>
<td id="mwDVY"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1641" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"U+3008 (12296)"},"2":{"wt":"U+3009 (12297)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1641" id="mwDVg"><li>U+3008 (12296)</li><li>U+3009 (12297)</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwDVk"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1367478826" about="#mwt1643" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDVo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Comma-separated list/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cslist","href":"./Template:Cslist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&amp;amp;#x3008;"},"2":{"wt":"&amp;amp;#x3009;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><ul class="cslist" about="#mwt1643" id="mwDVs"><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>#x3008;</li><li><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>#x3009;</li></ul></td>
<td id="mwDVw">Single angle brackets<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1645" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDV0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"plainlist","href":"./Template:Plainlist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n* Korean: 홑화살괄호 (&apos;&apos;hothwasalgwalho&apos;&apos;)\n* Chinese: 書名號 (&apos;&apos;shū míng hào&apos;&apos;)\n"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1646" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="plainlist " about="#mwt1645" id="mwDV4">
<ul><li>Korean: 홑화살괄호 (<i>hothwasalgwalho</i>)</li>
<li>Chinese: 書名號 (<i>shū míng hào</i>)</li></ul>

</div></td>
<td id="mwDV8"><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1647" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDWA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"plainlist","href":"./Template:Plainlist"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n* Korean (sub-titles of books, titles of movies, plays, art)\n* [[Chinese language|Chinese]] (for book titles within book titles.)\n"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1648" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="plainlist " about="#mwt1647" id="mwDWE">
<ul><li>Korean (sub-titles of books, titles of movies, plays, art)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_language" title="Chinese language">Chinese</a> (for book titles within book titles.)</li></ul>

</div></td></tr>
</tbody></table>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwDWI" aria-labelledby="Quotation_dash"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Quotation_dash">Quotation dash</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: Quotation dash"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1649" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDWM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Dash#Horizontal bar"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1650" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1649" id="mwDWQ">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dash#Horizontal_bar" title="Dash">Dash §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Horizontal bar</a></div>
<p id="mwDWU">Another typographical style is to omit quotation marks for lines of dialogue, replacing them with an initial dash, as in lines from James Joyce's <i id="mwDWY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulysses_(novel)" title="Ulysses (novel)" id="mwDWc">Ulysses</a></i>:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1651" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDWg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"block indent","href":"./Template:Block_indent"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"― O saints above! Miss Douce said, sighed above her jumping rose. I wished I hadn&apos;t laughed so much. I feel all wet.&lt;br />\n― O Miss Douce! Miss Kennedy protested. You horrid thing!&lt;ref>{{cite book |last=Joyce |first=James |title=Ulysses |date=1922 |publisher=The Bodley Head |location=London |at=p. 335, lines 7–11}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1652" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent " about="#mwt1651" id="mwDWk">― O saints above! Miss Douce said, sighed above her jumping rose. I wished I hadn't laughed so much. I feel all wet.<br/>
― O Miss Douce! Miss Kennedy protested. You horrid thing!<sup about="#mwt1655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwDWo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWw">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDW0">]</span></span></a></sup></div>

<p id="mwDW4">This style is particularly common in Bulgarian, French, Greek, Hungarian, Polish, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Spanish, Swedish, Turkish, and Vietnamese.<sup about="#mwt1658" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Vietnamese_109-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Vietnamese"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Vietnamese-109" id="mwDW8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXE">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXI">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwDXM">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_language" title="Finnish language" id="mwDXQ">Finnish</a>, the beginning of a reporting clause is marked only by the punctuation already existing in the sentence, or (if there was none) by adding a comma. When a quote continues after the reporting clause, the clause ends with a comma, and the continuation begins with another dash:<sup about="#mwt1661" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwDXU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXc">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXg">]</span></span></a></sup></p> <!-- The "English translation formatted in Finnish quotation style" rows below don't come from this source, they're just Wikipedia editorializing for the benefit of the reader. -->
<table class="wikitable    " about="#mwt1663" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwDXo" data-mw='{"attribs":[[{"txt":"class","html":"&lt;span about=\"#mwt1662\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDXk\" data-mw=&apos;{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Table\",\"href\":\"./Template:Table\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}&apos;>class=\"wikitable    \"&lt;/span>"},{"html":""}]]}'>
<tbody id="mwDXs"><tr id="mwDXw">
<th id="mwDX0">Finnish example</th>
<td id="mwDX4">– Et sinä ole paljon minkään näköinen, sanoi Korkala melkein surullisesti, – mutta ei auta.</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDX8">
<th id="mwDYA">English translation</th>
<td id="mwDYE">"You don't seem to be anything special," said Korkala almost sadly, "but there's no help to it."</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDYI">
<th id="mwDYM">English translation formatted in Finnish quotation style</th>
<td id="mwDYQ">– You don't seem to be anything special, said Korkala almost sadly, – but there's no help to it.</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDYU">
<td colspan="2" id="mwDYY"></td></tr>
<tr id="mwDYc">
<th id="mwDYg">Finnish example</th>
<td id="mwDYk">– Frakki, älähti Huikari. – Missä on frakki?<br id="mwDYo"/>– Räätälissä, sanoi Joonas rauhallisesti.</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDYs">
<th id="mwDYw">English translation</th>
<td id="mwDY0">"Tailcoat", yelped Huikari. "Where is the tailcoat?"<br id="mwDY4"/>"At the tailor's", said Joonas calmly.</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDY8">
<th id="mwDZA">English translation formatted in Finnish quotation style</th>
<td id="mwDZE">– Tailcoat, yelped Huikari. – Where is the tailcoat?<br id="mwDZI"/>– At the tailor's, said Joonas calmly.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwDZM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwDZQ">Unicode</a> standard introduced a separate character <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1664" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDZU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2015"},"2":{"wt":"HORIZONTAL BAR"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r886049734" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt1665" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .monospaced{font-family:monospace,monospace}</style><span class="monospaced">U+2015</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1664"><span typeof="mw:Entity">―</span></span><span about="#mwt1664"> </span><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1373397503" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt1664" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .unichar-name{font-variant:small-caps;text-transform:lowercase;font-feature-settings:"onum"}</style><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1664" id="mwDZY">HORIZONTAL BAR</span> to be used as a quotation dash.<sup about="#mwt1669" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwDZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZk">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwDZs" aria-labelledby="Electronic_documents"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Electronic_documents">Electronic documents</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: Electronic documents"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwDZw">Different <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typeface" title="Typeface" id="mwDZ0">typefaces</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_encoding" title="Character encoding" id="mwDZ4">character encodings</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_language" title="Computer language" id="mwDZ8">computer languages</a> use various encodings and glyphs for quotation marks.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwDaA" aria-labelledby="Typewriters_and_early_computers"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Typewriters_and_early_computers">Typewriters and early computers <span class="anchor" id="straight_quotation_marks"></span></h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: Typewriters and early computers "><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwDaE">On most keyboards, typographical quotation marks are absent.</p>

<p id="mwDaI">When typewriter keyboards were designed, curved quotation marks were not implemented. Instead, to limit the number of characters (and keys) required, straight quotation marks were invented as a compromise. At that time typesetting <i id="mwDaM">did</i> use curved quotation marks.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1670" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDaQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cn","href":"./Template:Cn"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_August_2025" about="#mwt1670"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1670" id="mwDaU"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2025)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASCII" title="ASCII" id="mwDaY">ASCII</a> character set, which has been used on a wide variety of computers since the 1960s, contains the straight versions only (<span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1671" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDac" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"0027"},"2":{"wt":"apostrophe"},"nlink":{"wt":"apostrophe"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1672" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+0027</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1671"><span typeof="mw:Entity">'</span></span><span about="#mwt1671"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1671" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1671" id="mwDag"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apostrophe" title="Apostrophe">APOSTROPHE</a></span> and <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1674" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDak" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"0022"},"2":{"wt":"quotation mark"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1675" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+0022</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1674"><span typeof="mw:Entity">"</span></span><span about="#mwt1674"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1674" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1674" id="mwDao">QUOTATION MARK</span>). All other forms of quotation marks, such as angled, lowered, inverted, were not provided by British or American typewriters.</p>

<p id="mwDas">Many systems, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_computer" title="Personal computer" id="mwDaw">personal computers</a> of the 1980s and early 1990s, actually drew these ASCII quotes like closing quotes (or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_(symbol)" title="Prime (symbol)" id="mwDa0">primes</a>) on-screen and in printouts, so text would <i id="mwDa4">appear</i> like this (approximately): </p>
<!-- Editors: please do not change these prime and grave characters to straight quotes, despite the Manual of Style. They have been used deliberately, to illustrate the point being made. -->

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1677" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDa8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"monodiv","href":"./Template:Monodiv"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{block indent|1=\n″Good morning, Dave,″ said HAL.&lt;!-- Double-prime character used for illustration -->&lt;br />\n′Good morning, Dave,′ said HAL.&lt;!-- Prime character used for illustration -->\n}} "}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1678" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="monospaced" about="#mwt1677" id="mwDbA">
<span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1679" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent ">″Good morning, Dave,″ said HAL.<br/>
′Good morning, Dave,′ said HAL.</div> </div>

<p id="mwDbE">These same systems often drew the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backtick" title="Backtick" id="mwDbI">backtick</a> (the free standing character <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1680" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDbM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"0060"},"2":{"wt":"grave accent"},"nlink":{"wt":"backtick"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1681" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+0060</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1680"><span typeof="mw:Entity">`</span></span><span about="#mwt1680"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1680" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1680" id="mwDbQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backtick" title="Backtick">GRAVE ACCENT</a></span>) as an 'open quote' glyph (usually a mirror image so it still sloped in the direction of a grave accent). Using this character as the opening quote gave a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typographic_approximation" title="Typographic approximation" id="mwDbU">typographic approximation</a> of curved single quotes. Nothing similar was available for the double quote, so many people resorted to using two single quotes for double quotes, which would <i id="mwDbY">look</i> approximately like the following:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1683" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDbc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"monodiv","href":"./Template:Monodiv"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{block indent|1=\n``Good morning, Dave,′′ said HAL.&lt;!-- Grave and prime characters used for illustration -->&lt;br />\n`Good morning, Dave,′ said HAL.&lt;!-- Grave and prime characters used for illustration -->\n}} "}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1684" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="monospaced" about="#mwt1683" id="mwDbg">
<span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1685" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent ">``Good morning, Dave,′′ said HAL.<br/>
`Good morning, Dave,′ said HAL.</div> </div>

<p id="mwDbk">The typesetting application <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TeX" title="TeX" id="mwDbo">TeX</a> uses this convention for input files. The following is an example of TeX input which yields proper curly quotation marks.</p>

<dl id="mwDbs"><dd id="mwDbw"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1686" id="mwDb0" data-mw='{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"text","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"``Good morning, Dave,&apos;&apos; said HAL."},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"``Good morning, Dave,&lt;nowiki>&apos;&apos;&lt;/nowiki> said HAL."}},"i":0}}]}'>``Good morning, Dave,'' said HAL.</code></dd>
<dd id="mwDb4"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1688" id="mwDb8" data-mw='{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"text","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"`Good morning, Dave,&apos; said HAL."},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"`Good morning, Dave,&apos; said HAL."}},"i":0}}]}'>`Good morning, Dave,' said HAL.</code></dd></dl>

<p id="mwDcA">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwDcE">Unicode</a> standard added <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codepoint" title="Codepoint" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDcI">codepoints</a> for slanted or curved quotes (<span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1690" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDcM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"201C"},"2":{"wt":"left double quotation mark"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1691" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+201C</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1690"><span typeof="mw:Entity">“</span></span><span about="#mwt1690"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1690" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1690" id="mwDcQ">LEFT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK</span> and <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1693" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDcU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"201D"},"2":{"wt":"right double quotation mark"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1694" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+201D</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:125%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1693"><span typeof="mw:Entity">”</span></span><span about="#mwt1693"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1693" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1693" id="mwDcY">RIGHT DOUBLE QUOTATION MARK</span>, described further below), shown here for comparison:</p>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1696" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDcc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"monodiv","href":"./Template:Monodiv"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"{{block indent|1=\n“Good morning, Dave,” said HAL.&lt;br />\n‘Good morning, Dave,’ said HAL.\n}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1697" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="monospaced" about="#mwt1696" id="mwDcg">
<span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r996643573" about="#mwt1698" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Block indent/styles.css"}}'/></span><div class="block-indent ">“Good morning, Dave,” said HAL.<br/>
‘Good morning, Dave,’ said HAL.</div></div>

<p id="mwDck">The Unicode mapping for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PostScript_Standard_Encoding" title="PostScript Standard Encoding" id="mwDco">PostScript Standard Encoding</a> preserves the typographic approximation convention by mapping its equivalent of ASCII grave and single-quote to the Unicode curly quotation mark characters.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwDcs" aria-labelledby="Keyboard_layouts"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Keyboard_layouts">Keyboard layouts</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25" title="Edit section: Keyboard layouts"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwDcw">Early computer keyboards copied layouts that had been established by typewriter keyboards. Most computer keyboards do not have specific keys for curved quotation marks or angled quotation marks. This may also have to do with computer character sets:</p>
<ul id="mwDc0"><li id="mwDc4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_page#IBM_PC_/_DOS_(OEM)_code_pages" title="Code page" id="mwDc8">IBM character sets</a> generally do not include curved quotation mark characters, therefore, keys for those marks are absent from most IBM computer keyboards.<sup about="#mwt1699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdI">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDdQ">Microsoft followed the example of IBM in its character set and keyboard design. Curved quotation marks were implemented later in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_code_page" title="Windows code page" id="mwDdU">Windows character sets</a>, but most Microsoft computer keyboards<sup about="#mwt1724" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwDdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdg">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdk">]</span></span></a></sup> do not have a dedicated key for the curved quotation mark characters. On keyboards with the <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1249182868" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1700" id="mwDdo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Key press/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Key press","href":"./Template:Key_press"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alt Gr"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .keyboard-key{border:1px solid #aaa;border-radius:0.2em;box-shadow:0.1em 0.1em 0.2em rgba(0,0,0,0.1);background-color:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#f8f9fa);background-image:linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--background-color-neutral,#eaecf0),var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#f8f9fa),var(--background-color-neutral,#eaecf0));color:var(--color-base,#202122);padding:0.1em 0.3em;font-family:inherit;font-size:0.85em}</style><kbd class="keyboard-key nowrap" about="#mwt1700" id="mwDds">Alt Gr</kbd> key or both the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1249182868" about="#mwt1702" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDdw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Key press/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Key press","href":"./Template:Key_press"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alt"}},"i":0}}]}'/><kbd class="keyboard-key nowrap" about="#mwt1702" id="mwDd0">Alt</kbd> key and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numeric_keypad" title="Numeric keypad" id="mwDd4">numeric keypad</a>, they are accessible through a series of keystrokes that involve these keys.<sup about="#mwt1704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Using the [[numeric keypad]], {{Key press|Alt|0}}{{Key press|1|4|5|chain=}} through {{Key press|Alt|0}}{{Key press|1|4|8|chain=}} yield, respectively, {{char|‘}}, {{char|’}},  {{char|“}}, and {{char|”}}.&lt;ref>{{cite web|url= https://fsymbols.com/keyboard/windows/alt-codes/list/|title=Alt codes list ☺♥♪ keyboard symbols|website=fsymbols.com|last=Méñshykov|first=Ihor|access-date=8 June 2020}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-128" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDd8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDeA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeE">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeI">]</span></span></a></sup>  Also, techniques using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Unicode_code_point_table" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwDeM">their Unicode code points</a> are available; see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode_input#Hexadecimal_code_input" title="Unicode input" id="mwDeQ">Unicode input</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDeU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_page#Apple_related_code_pages" title="Code page" id="mwDeY">Macintosh character sets</a> have always had curved quotation marks available. Nevertheless, these are mostly only accessible through a series of keystrokes involving the <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1249182868" about="#mwt1725" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDec" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Key press/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Key press","href":"./Template:Key_press"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Opt"}},"i":0}}]}'/><kbd class="keyboard-key nowrap" about="#mwt1725" id="mwDeg">⌥ Opt</kbd> key.</li></ul>

<p id="mwDek">In languages that use the curved <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDeo">“...”</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1727" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-keyboard-129"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""},"1":{"wt":"in 1st or 2nd level access, i.e., specific key or using the {{Key press|Shift}} key; not 3rd or 4th level access, i.e., using {{Key press|Alt Gr}} key or {{Key press|Opt}} key, in conjunction or not with the {{Key press|Shift}} key."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDe0">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDe4">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDe8"><li id="mwDfA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_(keyboard_layout)" title="Neo (keyboard layout)" id="mwDfE">Neo</a></li></ul>

<p id="mwDfI">In languages that use angular <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDfM">«...»</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1738" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDfQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfY">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfc">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDfg"><li id="mwDfk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabic_keyboard#Mac_Arabic_Keyboard" title="Arabic keyboard" id="mwDfo">Macintosh Arabic keyboard</a>;<sup about="#mwt1743" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Unicode-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDf0">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDf4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDf8">Armenian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgI">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ibmkbd-125"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgY">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwDgg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgo">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDgw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QWERTY#Canadian_French" title="QWERTY" id="mwDg0">Canadian keyboard</a><sup about="#mwt1751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhA">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1752" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDhI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhQ">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1755" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwDhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhg">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDho">French <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BÉPO" title="BÉPO" id="mwDhs">BÉPO</a> keyboard<sup about="#mwt1758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwDhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDh0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDh4">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDh8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDiA">Greek keyboard<sup about="#mwt1759" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDiE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDiI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiM">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1760" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDiU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDiY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDic">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDig">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1763" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwDik"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDio"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDis">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDi0">Khmer keyboard<sup about="#mwt1764" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDi4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDi8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjA">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDjI">Latvian ergonomic keyboard<sup about="#mwt1765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjU">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1766" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDjc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjk">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1769" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135"}}'><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwDjs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDj0">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDj4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDj8">Pashto keyboard<sup about="#mwt1770" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkI">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1773" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-136" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136"}}'><a href="#cite_note-136" id="mwDkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkY">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDkg">Persian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1774" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDkk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDko"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDks">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1775" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDk0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDk4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDk8">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwDlE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlM">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDlU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_keyboard_layout" title="Portuguese keyboard layout" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDlY">Portuguese keyboard</a><sup about="#mwt1779" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDlc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlk">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1780" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDls"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDl0">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDl4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1783" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwDl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmE">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDmM">Syriac keyboard<sup about="#mwt1784" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDmQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmY">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1787" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwDmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmo">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDms">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDmw">Uyghur keyboard<sup about="#mwt1788" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDm0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDm4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDm8">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1791" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-140" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-140" id="mwDnE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDnI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnM">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDnU">In languages that use the corner bracket <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDnY">「...」</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1792" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDnc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnk">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDno">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDns"><li id="mwDnw">Japanese keyboard<sup about="#mwt1795" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDn0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDn4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn8">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1796" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDoE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoM">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDoU">In languages that use the angle bracket <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDoY">《...》</span><sup about="#mwt1797" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mongolian_141-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mongolian","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-mongolian-141"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"mongolian\""},"1":{"wt":"These should be rotated 90 degrees in vertical text."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-mongolian-141" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDoc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDog"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDok">[</span>e<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoo">]</span></span></a></sup> they are available in:</p>
<ul id="mwDos"><li id="mwDow">Mongolian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1800" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDo0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDo4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDo8">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1803" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-142" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-142" id="mwDpE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpM">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDpU">New Tai Lue keyboard<sup about="#mwt1804" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDpY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpg">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpk">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDpo">In languages that use the curved <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDps">„...“</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1805" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDp0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDp4">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDp8">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDqA"><li id="mwDqE">Bulgarian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1808" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDqI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqQ">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1811" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143"}}'><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwDqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqg">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDqo">Georgian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1812" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDqs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDq0">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDq4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1813" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ibmkbd_125-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ibmkbd"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ibmkbd-125" id="mwDq8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrE">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1816" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-144" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-144"}}'><a href="#cite_note-144" id="mwDrM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrU">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDrc">Macedonian keyboard<sup about="#mwt1817" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDro">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1820" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-145" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-145"}}'><a href="#cite_note-145" id="mwDrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr4">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr8">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDsA">In languages that use the curved <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDsE">„...”</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1821" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDsI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsQ">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsU">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDsY"><li id="mwDsc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_keyboard_layout" title="Romanian keyboard layout" id="mwDsg">Romanian Standard SR 13392:2004 keyboard</a><sup about="#mwt1824" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Unicode_130-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Unicode"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Unicode-130" id="mwDsk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDso"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDss">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-146" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-146"}}'><a href="#cite_note-146" id="mwDs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDs8">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDtE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_(keyboard_layout)" title="Neo (keyboard layout)" id="mwDtI">Neo</a></li></ul>

<p id="mwDtM">In languages that use the curved <span style="font-family:serif; font-size:x-large" id="mwDtQ">”...”</span> quotation marks, they are available<sup about="#mwt1828" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-keyboard_129-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"keyboard","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"\"keyboard\""}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-keyboard-129" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDtU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDtY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtc">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtg">]</span></span></a></sup> in:</p>
<ul id="mwDtk"><li id="mwDto">none</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="26" id="mwDts" aria-labelledby="Curved_quotes_within_and_across_applications"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Curved_quotes_within_and_across_applications">Curved quotes within and across applications</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26" title="Edit section: Curved quotes within and across applications"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDtw">Historically, support for curved quotes was a problem in information technology, primarily because the widely used ASCII character set did not include a representation for them.<sup about="#mwt1831" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-147" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\n[[Unicode and email|To use non ASCII characters in e-mail]] and on [[Usenet]] the sending mail application generally needs to set a [[MIME type]] specifying the encoding. In most cases (the exceptions being if [[UTF-7]] is used or if the [[8BITMIME]] extension is present), this also requires the use of a [[MIME#Content-Transfer-Encoding|content-transfer encoding]]. &lt;!--Could not find any reference. A few mail clients send curved quotes using the [[windows-1252]] codes, but mark the text as ISO-8859-1, causing problems for decoders that do not make the dubious assumption that C1 [[control code]]s in ISO-8859-1 text were meant to be windows-1252 printable characters.-->([[Mozilla Thunderbird]] allows insertion of [[HTML]] code such as {{code|‘}} and {{code|”}} to produce typographic quotation marks; see [[#Unicode code point table|below]].)"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-147" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDt0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDt4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDt8">[</span>f<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDuE">The term "smart quotes", <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1838" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDuI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"“...”"}},"i":0}}]}'>“...”</span>, is from the name in several word processors of a function aimed this problem: automatically converting straight quotes typed by the user into curved quotes, the feature attempts to be "smart" enough to determine whether the punctuation marked opening or closing. Since curved quotes are the typographically correct ones,<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1839" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDuM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"June 2021"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_June_2021" about="#mwt1839"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1839" id="mwDuQ"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (June 2021)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> word processors have traditionally offered curved quotes to users (at minimum as available characters). Before <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode" title="Unicode" id="mwDuU">Unicode</a> was widely accepted and supported, this meant representing the curved quotes in whatever 8-bit encoding the software and underlying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operating_system" title="Operating system" id="mwDuY">operating system</a> was using. The character sets for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows" title="Microsoft Windows" id="mwDuc">Windows</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Macintosh" title="Apple Macintosh" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDug">Macintosh</a> used two different pairs of values for curved quotes, while <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8859-1" title="ISO 8859-1" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDuk">ISO 8859-1</a> (historically the default character set for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix" title="Unix" id="mwDuo">Unixes</a> and older <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux" title="Linux" id="mwDus">Linux</a> systems) has <i id="mwDuw">no</i> curved quotes, making cross-platform and cross-application compatibility difficult.</p>

<p id="mwDu0">Performance by these "smart quotes" features was far from perfect overall (variance potential by e.g. subject matter, formatting/style convention, user typing habits). As many word processors (including Microsoft Word and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenOffice.org" title="OpenOffice.org" id="mwDu4">OpenOffice.org</a>) have the function enabled by default, users may not have realized that the ASCII-compatible straight quotes they were typing on their keyboards ended up as something different (conversely users could incorrectly assume its functioning in other applications, e.g. composing emails).</p>

<p id="mwDu8">The curved <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apostrophe" title="Apostrophe" id="mwDvA">apostrophe</a> is the same character as the closing single quote.<sup about="#mwt1843" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-148" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-148"}}'><a href="#cite_note-148" id="mwDvE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvM">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvQ">]</span></span></a></sup> "Smart quotes" features wrongly convert initial apostrophes (as in 'tis, 'em, 'til, and '89) into <i id="mwDvU">opening</i> single quotes. (An example of this error appears in the advertisements for the television show <i id="mwDvY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/'Til_Death" title="'Til Death" id="mwDvc">'Til Death</a></i>.) The two very different functions of this character can cause confusion, particularly in British styles,<sup about="#mwt1840" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GB_149-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GB","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GB-149"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"group":{"wt":"35em"},"name":{"wt":"GB"},"1":{"wt":"[[UK English]], [[Scots Gaelic]] and [[Welsh language|Welsh]] as described in the article."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-GB-149" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDvg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvo">[</span>g<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvs">]</span></span></a></sup> in which single quotes are the standard primary.</p>

<p id="mwDvw">Unicode support has since become the norm for operating systems. Thus, in at least some cases, transferring content containing curved quotes (or any other non-ASCII characters) from a word processor to another application or platform has been less troublesome, provided all steps in the process (including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clipboard_(software)" title="Clipboard (software)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDv0">clipboard</a> if applicable) are Unicode-aware. But there are still applications which still use the older character sets, or output data using them, and thus problems still occur.</p>

<p id="mwDv4">There are other considerations for including curved quotes in the widely used <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markup_language" title="Markup language" id="mwDv8">markup languages</a> HTML, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML" title="XML" id="mwDwA">XML</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SGML" title="SGML" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDwE">SGML</a>. If the encoding of the document supports direct representation of the characters, they can be used, but doing so can cause difficulties if the document needs to be edited by someone who is using an editor that cannot support the encoding. For example, many simple text editors only handle a few encodings or assume that the encoding of any file opened is a platform default, so the quote characters may appear as the generic replacement character <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1844" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDwI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"�"}},"i":0}}]}'>�</span> or "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojibake" title="Mojibake" id="mwDwM">mojibake</a>" (gibberish). HTML includes a set of entities for curved quotes: <code id="mwDwQ"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDwU">&amp;</span>lsquo;</code> (left single), <code id="mwDwY"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDwc">&amp;</span>rsquo;</code> (right single or apostrophe), <code id="mwDwg"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDwk">&amp;</span>sbquo;</code> (low 9 single), <code id="mwDwo"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDws">&amp;</span>ldquo;</code> (left double), <code id="mwDww"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDw0">&amp;</span>rdquo;</code> (right double), and <code id="mwDw4"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDw8">&amp;</span>bdquo;</code> (low 9 double). XML does not define these by default, but specifications based on it can do so, and XHTML does. In addition, while the HTML 4, XHTML and XML specifications allow specifying numeric character references in either hexadecimal or decimal, SGML and older versions of HTML (and many old implementations) only support decimal references. Thus, to represent curly quotes in XML and SGML, it is safest to use the decimal numeric character references. That is, to represent the double curly quotes use <code id="mwDxA"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDxE">&amp;</span>#8220;</code> and <code id="mwDxI"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDxM">&amp;</span>#8221;</code>, and to represent single curly quotes use <code id="mwDxQ"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDxU">&amp;</span>#8216;</code> and <code id="mwDxY"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDxc">&amp;</span>#8217;</code>. Both numeric and named references function correctly in almost every modern browser. While using numeric references can make a page more compatible with outdated browsers, using named references are safer for systems that handle multiple character encodings (i.e. RSS aggregators and search results).</p>

<p id="mwDxg">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows" title="Windows" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDxk">Windows</a> file and folder names, the straight double quotation mark is prohibited, as it is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reserved_character" title="Reserved character" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDxo">reserved character</a>.  The curved quotation marks, as well as the straight single quotation mark, are permitted.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="27" id="mwDxs" aria-labelledby="Usenet_and_email"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Usenet_and_email">Usenet and email</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27" title="Edit section: Usenet and email"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwDxw">The style of quoting known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usenet_quoting" title="Usenet quoting" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDx0">Usenet quoting</a> uses the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater-than_sign" title="Greater-than sign" id="mwDx4">greater-than sign</a>, <span class="nounderlines" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color-muted,#ddd); color: var(--color-base,#202122); background-color: var( --background-color-neutral-subtle, #fdfdfd); padding: 1px 1px;" about="#mwt1845" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDx8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"char","href":"./Template:Char"},"params":{"1":{"wt":">"}},"i":0}}]}'>></span> prepended to a line of text to mark it as a quote. This convention was later standardized in <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1333433106" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1846" id="mwDyA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"IETF RFC","href":"./Template:IETF_RFC"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"3676"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:"\"""\"""'""'"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration.id-lock-registration a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Lock-gray-alt-2.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription.id-lock-subscription a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Lock-red-alt-2.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Wikisource-logo.svg")right 0.1em center/12px no-repeat}body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-free a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background-size:contain;padding:0 1em 0 0}.mw-parser-output .cs1-code{color:inherit;background:inherit;border:none;padding:inherit}.mw-parser-output .cs1-hidden-error{display:none;color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-visible-error{color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{display:none;color:#085;margin-left:0.3em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-left{padding-left:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-right{padding-right:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .citation .mw-selflink{font-weight:inherit}@media screen{.mw-parser-output .cs1-format{font-size:95%}html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}</style><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RFC_(identifier)" title="RFC (identifier)" about="#mwt1846" class="mw-redirect">RFC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1846"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3676" about="#mwt1846" class="external text">3676</a>, and was adopted subsequently by many email clients when automatically including quoted text from previous messages (in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_text" title="Plain text" id="mwDyE">plain text</a> mode).</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="28" id="mwDyI" aria-labelledby="Unicode_code_point_table"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Unicode_code_point_table"><span class="anchor" id="Quotation_marks_in_Unicode"></span> Unicode code point table</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Quotation_mark&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28" title="Edit section:  Unicode code point table"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwDyM">In Unicode, 30 characters are marked <code id="mwDyQ">Quotation Mark=Yes</code> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode_character_property" title="Unicode character property" id="mwDyU">character property</a>.<sup about="#mwt1850" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-150" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150"}}'><a href="#cite_note-150" id="mwDyY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyg">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyk">]</span></span></a></sup> They all have general category "Punctuation", and a subcategory Open, Close, Initial, Final or Other (<code id="mwDyo">Ps, Pe, Pi, Pf, Po</code>). Several other Unicode characters with quotation mark semantics lack the character property.</p>
<table class="wikitable" id="unicode_quote_table">
<tbody class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwDys"><tr class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwDyw"></tr>
</tbody><caption id="mwDy0">Quotation marks in Unicode <small id="mwDy4">(<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode_character_property" title="Unicode character property" id="mwDy8">Character property</a> "Quotation_Mark"=Yes)</small></caption>
<tbody id="mwDzA"><tr id="mwDzE">
<th id="mwDzI">Character</th><th id="mwDzM">Comments</th></tr>
<tr id="mwDzQ">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwDzU"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1851" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDzY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"0022"},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1852" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+0022</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1851"><span typeof="mw:Entity">"</span></span><span about="#mwt1851"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1851" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1851">QUOTATION MARK</span><span about="#mwt1851"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1851" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1851"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>quot;, <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>QUOT;</span><span about="#mwt1851">)</span></td>
<td id="mwDzc">Typewriter ("programmer's") quote, ambidextrous. Also known as "double quote".</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDzg">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwDzk"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1855" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDzo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"0027"},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1856" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+0027</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1855"><span typeof="mw:Entity">'</span></span><span about="#mwt1855"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1855" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1855">APOSTROPHE</span><span about="#mwt1855"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1855" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1855"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>apos;</span><span about="#mwt1855">)</span></td>
<td id="mwDzs">Typewriter ("programmer's") straight single quote, ambidextrous</td></tr>
<tr id="mwDzw">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwDz0"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1859" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDz4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"00AB  "},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1860" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+00AB</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1859"><span typeof="mw:Entity">«</span></span><span about="#mwt1859"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1859" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1859">LEFT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK</span><span about="#mwt1859"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1859" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1859"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>laquo;</span><span about="#mwt1859">)</span></td>
<td id="mwDz8">Double angle quote (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevron_(insignia)" title="Chevron (insignia)" id="mwD0A">chevron</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillemets" title="Guillemets" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD0E">guillemet</a>, duck-foot quote), left</td></tr>
<tr id="mwD0I">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwD0M"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1863" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD0Q" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"00BB "},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1864" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+00BB</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1863"><span typeof="mw:Entity">»</span></span><span about="#mwt1863"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1863" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1863">RIGHT-POINTING DOUBLE ANGLE QUOTATION MARK</span><span about="#mwt1863"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1863" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1863"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>raquo;</span><span about="#mwt1863">)</span></td>
<td id="mwD0U">Double angle quote, right</td></tr>
<tr id="mwD0Y">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwD0c"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1867" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD0g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2018 "},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1868" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+2018</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1867"><span typeof="mw:Entity">‘</span></span><span about="#mwt1867"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1867" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1867">LEFT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK</span><span about="#mwt1867"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1867" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1867"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>lsquo;, <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>OpenCurlyQuote;</span><span about="#mwt1867">)</span></td>
<td id="mwD0k">Single curved quote, left. Also known as <i id="mwD0o">inverted <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comma" title="Comma" id="mwD0s">comma</a></i> or <i id="mwD0w">turned comma</i><sup about="#mwt1871" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-152" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-152"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Also sometimes used by 18th- and 19th-century printers for the small \"c\" for Scottish names, e.g. {{char|M‘Culloch}} rather than {{char|M&lt;sup>c&lt;/sup>Culloch}}.&lt;ref>{{cite web\n |url= http://www.greenbag.org/v12n3/v12n3_collins.pdf |title=M&apos;Culloch and the Turned Comma |publisher=The Green Bag Inc. |access-date=7 January 2014 |archive-date=24 September 2015 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20150924023612/http://www.greenbag.org/v12n3/v12n3_collins.pdf |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref> For a printed example see the Green Bag reference or the [[s:Page:The Dictionary of Australasian Biography.djvu/306|Dictionary of Australasian Biography, page 290]] (Wikisource)."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-152" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwD00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD08">[</span>h<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1A">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
<tr id="mwD1E">
<td style="text-align:center;" id="mwD1I"><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1881" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD1M" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"unichar","href":"./Template:Unichar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2019 "},"size":{"wt":"180%"},"nlink":{"wt":"Right single quotation mark"},"html":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1882" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced">U+2019</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span><span style="font-size:180%;line-height:1em" about="#mwt1881"><span typeof="mw:Entity">’</span></span><span about="#mwt1881"> </span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1373397503" about="#mwt1881" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Unichar/name/styles.css"}}'/><span class="unichar-name" about="#mwt1881"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Right_single_quotation_mark" title="Right single quotation mark">RIGHT SINGLE QUOTATION MARK</a></span><span about="#mwt1881"> (</span><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r886049734" about="#mwt1881" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Mono/styles.css"}}'/><span class="monospaced" about="#mwt1881"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>CloseCurlyQuote;, <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>rsquo;, <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span>rsquor;</span><span about="#mwt1881">)</span></td>
<td id="mwD1Q">Single curved quote, right<sup about="#mwt1885" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"The same U+2019 [[code point]] and glyph is used for typographic (curly) [[apostrophe]]s. Both [[#Typewriter quotation marks|U+0027]] and U+2019 are ambiguous about distinguishing punctuation from apostrophes."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-153" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwD1U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1c">[</span>i<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1g">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
<tr id="mwD1k">
